{"ports":[{"code":"GRPMS","name":"Patmos","arrivalMode":"tender","photoUrl":"./media/files/port-GRPMS.webp","about":{"en":"Small, quiet Patmos is where St John is said to have written the Book of Revelation. The hilltop monastery and the village of Chora, with the cave, are a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The ship anchors offshore and guests go ashore by tender.","tr":"Küçük ve sakin Patmos, Aziz Yuhanna'nın Vahiy'i yazdığı ada olarak bilinir. Tepedeki manastır ve Chora köyü, mağarayla birlikte UNESCO Dünya Mirası'dır. Gemimiz açıkta demirler, karaya tender botlarla çıkılır."}},{"code":"GRRHO","name":"Rodos","arrivalMode":"dock","photoUrl":"./media/files/port-GRRHO.webp","about":{"en":"Rhodes, the Island of the Sun, is the largest of the Dodecanese. The Knights' walled medieval town is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and on the east coast the white village of Lindos rises below its acropolis.","tr":"Güneş Adası Rodos, Oniki Adalar'ın en büyüğü. Şövalyelerin surlarla çevrili ortaçağ şehri UNESCO Dünya Mirası listesinde; adanın doğusunda beyaz evli Lindos ve akropolisi yükselir."}},{"code":"GRSMI","name":"Samos","arrivalMode":"tender","photoUrl":"./media/files/port-GRSMI.webp","about":{"en":"Samos, home of Pythagoras and Epicurus, is known for its green mountains, Muscat wine and the ancient town of Pythagorion. Pythagorion and the Heraion are a UNESCO World Heritage Site.","tr":"Pisagor'un ve Epikür'ün adası Samos; yeşil dağları, Muskat şarabı ve antik Pythagorion kentiyle bilinir. Pythagorion ve Hera Tapınağı UNESCO Dünya Mirası listesindedir."}},{"code":"TRCES","name":"Çeşme","arrivalMode":"dock","photoUrl":"./media/files/port-TRCES.webp"}],"scenes":{"sea_day":"./media/files/sea_day.webp","sea_night":"./media/files/sea_night.webp","forced":"sea_day"},"guide":[{"id":"3fb6df6c-37df-4acb-98d1-f507a9444735","kind":"excursion","portCode":"GRPMS","category":"culture","emoji":"⛪","title":{"en":"Cave of the Apocalypse and St John's Monastery","tr":"Vahiy Mağarası ve Aziz Yuhan